  "creating-a-rideable-animal/vehicle": {
    "title": "Creating a rideable animal/vehicle",
    "groups": [
      {
        "heading": null,
        "rows": [
          [
            "Data1",
            "•\thead, neck and headnub exactly where the game expects them. You do not need to rig any vertices to them."
          ],
          [
            "Data2",
            "•\tThe riding bone mid-back. This is renamed ‘Bip01 L UpperArm’ and the original L upperarm needs to be renamed something else, fe. Bip01 L UpperArm 001"
          ],
          [
            "Data3",
            "•\ta cart bone."
          ],
          [
            "Data4",
            "•\tAny other extra bone you think you need. Please note, that every extra bone is a burden to the game engine and should only exist if you really need one. Fe. rhino horns on the snout do not need bones, as they move with the head. A tail would need 1-3 bones to move smoothly (most animal skeletons already include these)."
          ]
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
